{%- comment -%}
  AJ Daily Deal — the featured deal of the day.

  Resolves the active deal itself rather than making someone pick one every
  morning: it walks the `daily_deal` metaobject entries and takes the one whose
  start/end window contains "now". Queue a week of deals in advance and they
  rotate on their own.

  Requires a `daily_deal` metaobject definition with these fields:

    product             product_reference  the deal item
    starts_at           date_time          when it goes live
    ends_at             date_time          when it stops — drives the clock
    units_allocated     number_integer     units committed; NOT a cap — see aj-deal-claimed
    starting_inventory  number_integer     stock on hand at open; see below
    headline            single_line_text   optional eyebrow, e.g. "Today only"

  `starting_inventory` is what makes the sold count work on dropshipped
  products. The supplier holds the stock and it dwarfs any allocation we make,
  so the count measures the drop from this snapshot rather than assuming we
  started with our allocation on the shelf.

  Renders nothing on the storefront when no deal is active, so an empty queue
  degrades to an absent section rather than a broken one. In the theme editor it
  falls back to the first entry so there is something to design against.

  NOTE ON CACHING: the active-deal lookup happens server-side at render time. At
  a deal boundary a visitor may briefly see the outgoing deal from cache; the
  countdown is client-side against an absolute timestamp, so it stays correct
  regardless and hits zero on schedule.
{%- endcomment -%}

<script src="{{ 'aj-daily-deal.js' | asset_url }}" type="module" fetchpriority="low"></script>
<script src="{{ 'aj-variant-select.js' | asset_url }}" type="module" fetchpriority="low"></script>

{%- liquid
  assign now = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  assign deal = null

  for entry in shop.metaobjects.daily_deal.values
    assign starts = entry.starts_at.value | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign ends = entry.ends_at.value | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    if starts <= now and ends > now
      assign deal = entry
      break
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Editor-only fallback. Never applies on the live storefront — a merchant
    designing the section needs to see it, a customer must not see an expired
    or unstarted deal.
  endcomment
  if deal == null and request.design_mode
    assign deal = shop.metaobjects.daily_deal.values.first
  endif

  assign product = deal.product.value
  assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  comment
    The hero follows the picker, and the picker starts on `variant`. Rendering
    product.featured_image instead left the page opening on one colour while the
    dropdown named another — on this catalogue the deal product is often a
    single form in nine glazes, so the mismatch is the whole decision.

    NOT EVERY VARIANT HAS ITS OWN PHOTO. Suppliers shoot what they shoot: of the
    nine colours on the current deal, four have no image and two share one. So
    every lookup falls back to the product image rather than blanking, here and
    in the script.
  endcomment
  assign hero_image = variant.image | default: product.featured_image

  assign on_sale = false
  if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price
    assign on_sale = true
    assign savings = variant.compare_at_price | minus: variant.price
    assign savings_percent = savings | times: 100 | divided_by: variant.compare_at_price
  endif
-%}

{%- if product != blank -%}
  <div
    class="aj-deal color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} section spacing-style"
    style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
  >
    {%- comment -%}
      Marks how far the picker may reach to find the hero image. The picker sits
      in the info column and the image is in the media column, so it cannot just
      look inside its own row the way the cart upsell does.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="aj-deal__inner page-width" data-aj-variant-scope>
      {%- comment -%}
        The hero image loads EAGER, unlike everything else on the page. It is
        the largest element above the fold and the thing the whole homepage is
        about — lazy-loading it left a blank half-screen beside the price on
        first paint, and made the deal photo the page's LCP element arriving
        last. Every other image here stays lazy.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="aj-deal__media">
        {%- if hero_image -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The marker sits on the anchor, not the img: `image_tag` takes named
            arguments, and Liquid cannot parse a hyphenated one like
            `data-aj-variant-image:`.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <a href="{{ product.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" data-aj-variant-image>
            {{
              hero_image
              | image_url: width: 1200
              | image_tag:
                loading: 'eager',
                fetchpriority: 'high',
                sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 50vw, 100vw',
                widths: '400, 600, 800, 1000, 1200',
                class: 'aj-deal__image',
                alt: hero_image.alt
            }}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if on_sale -%}
          <span class="aj-deal__badge">Save {{ savings_percent }}%</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="aj-deal__content">
        {%- assign eyebrow = deal.headline.value | default: section.settings.default_headline -%}
        {%- if eyebrow != blank -%}
          <p class="aj-deal__eyebrow">{{ eyebrow | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <h2 class="aj-deal__title">
          <a href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title | escape }}</a>
        </h2>

        <div class="aj-deal__pricing">
          <span class="aj-deal__price" data-aj-upsell-price>{{ variant.price | money }}</span>
          {%- if on_sale -%}
            <s class="aj-deal__compare">{{ variant.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
            <span class="aj-deal__savings">You save {{ savings | money }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- if section.settings.show_countdown and deal.ends_at.value != blank -%}
          {% render 'aj-deal-countdown',
            ends_at: deal.ends_at.value,
            reload_on_expire: section.settings.reload_on_expire,
            heading: section.settings.countdown_heading
          %}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.show_claimed -%}
          {% render 'aj-deal-claimed',
            product: product,
            units_allocated: deal.units_allocated.value,
            starting_inventory: deal.starting_inventory.value,
            min_sold: settings.sold_min_count,
            label: settings.sold_label
          %}
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="aj-deal__cta" data-aj-upsell-row>
          {%- comment -%}
            Add to cart HERE, options and all. Sending someone to the product
            page to pick a colour loses most of them, and this is the one item on
            the site we most want bought — so the same picker the cart upsell
            uses appears inline instead.

            Built on Horizon's product-form-component, which posts to the cart,
            asks for the cart sections back and morphs them in. With
            auto_open_cart_drawer on, the drawer opens by itself.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if variant.available -%}
            {%- assign deal_form_id = 'AjDeal-' | append: product.id -%}

            {%- unless product.variants.size == 1 -%}
              <aj-variant-select class="aj-deal__variants">
                <label class="visually-hidden" for="{{ deal_form_id }}-variant">
                  Option for {{ product.title | escape }}
                </label>
                <select id="{{ deal_form_id }}-variant" class="aj-deal__select">
                  {%- for v in product.variants -%}
                    {%- assign v_image = v.image | default: product.featured_image -%}
                    <option
                      value="{{ v.id }}"
                      data-price="{{ v.price | money }}"
                      data-available="{{ v.available }}"
                      {%- if v_image %}
                        data-image-src="{{ v_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
                        data-image-srcset="{{ v_image | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w, {{ v_image | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w, {{ v_image | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w"
                        data-image-alt="{{ v_image.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
                      {%- endif %}
                      {% if v.id == variant.id %}selected{% endif %}
                      {% unless v.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
                    >
                      {{ v.title | escape }}
                      {%- unless v.available %} — sold out{% endunless -%}
                    </option>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
              </aj-variant-select>
            {%- endunless -%}

            <product-form-component
              data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
              data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
              on:submit="/handleSubmit"
              class="aj-deal__form-component"
            >
              <div
                class="visually-hidden"
                aria-live="assertive"
                role="status"
                aria-atomic="true"
                ref="liveRegion"
              ></div>
              {%- form 'product', product, id: deal_form_id, novalidate: 'novalidate', data-type: 'add-to-cart-form' -%}
                <input type="hidden" name="id" ref="variantId" value="{{ variant.id }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
                <button type="submit" class="button aj-deal__button">
                  {{ 'actions.add_to_cart' | t | default: 'Add to cart' }}
                </button>
              {%- endform -%}
            </product-form-component>

            <a href="{{ product.url }}" class="aj-deal__details">See full details</a>
          {%- else -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              A SOLD-OUT YOINK IS NOT A BROKEN PAGE, and until now it read like
              one: a bare "Sold out" under a countdown still ticking, on a
              product the homepage hero and every share still point at. The deal
              deliberately stays visible when it sells out — hiding it would 404
              the announcement bar, the Meta post and every link anyone shared —
              so the page has to say something worth reading for the rest of the
              window.

              This is the best available outcome from the worst case. Someone
              arriving at a sold-out deal has already shown they wanted it, so
              peak disappointment is also peak intent for "tell me about the
              next one" — which is exactly what the block below already offers.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <p class="aj-deal__soldout">
              <strong>Gone.</strong> Today's Yoink sold out.
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          BELOW the add-to-cart, deliberately. Its whole job is to catch someone
          who is not buying today, and between the price and the button it would
          interrupt the highest-intent moment on the site with a reason to leave.
          Here it is only reached by someone who scrolled past the button.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if settings.tomorrow_enabled -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The heading changes when the deal is gone. "Today's Yoink not your
            thing?" is addressed to someone who chose not to buy; to someone who
            could not, it reads as a taunt.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign peek_heading = settings.tomorrow_heading
            unless variant.available
              assign peek_heading = settings.soldout_heading | default: "Missed it? Here's what's next."
            endunless
          -%}
          {% render 'aj-deal-tomorrow',
            heading: peek_heading,
            show_signup: settings.tomorrow_signup
          %}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Editor-only setup hint. Customers never see this branch.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="aj-deal aj-deal--empty page-width">
    <p>
      <strong>No daily deal is set up yet.</strong>
      Create a <code>daily_deal</code> metaobject entry with a product,
      <code>starts_at</code>, <code>ends_at</code>, and
      <code>units_allocated</code>, and it will appear here automatically.
    </p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .aj-deal__inner {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--padding-lg, 2rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-deal__inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .aj-deal__media {
    position: relative;
  }

  .aj-deal__image {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .aj-deal__badge {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: var(--padding-sm, 1rem);
    inset-inline-start: var(--padding-sm, 1rem);
    padding: 0.3em 0.7em;
    border-radius: 3px;
    /* The grab colour, not the theme neutral. This badge is the single loudest
       claim on the homepage — the saving on today's Yoink — and it sat in plain
       ink because it predates the palette. Ink on yellow is 11.17:1, so it is
       both the loudest and the most readable pairing available. Falls back to
       the old neutral if the brand sheet ever fails to load. */
    background: var(--aj-price-accent, rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb)));
    color: var(--aj-price-on-accent, rgb(var(--color-background-rgb)));
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .aj-deal__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .aj-deal__title {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .aj-deal__title a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .aj-deal__pricing {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-block-end: var(--padding-md, 1.5rem);
  }

  .aj-deal__price {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .aj-deal__compare {
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .aj-deal__savings {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .aj-deal__cta {
    margin-block-start: var(--padding-md, 1.5rem);
  }

  .aj-deal__variants {
    display: block;
    margin-block-end: 0.6rem;
  }

  .aj-deal__select {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 22rem;
    padding: 0.55em 2em 0.55em 0.7em;
    border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.35);
    border-radius: 3px;
    background-color: transparent;
    color: inherit;
    font: inherit;
    /* Native arrows vary wildly by platform; draw our own so the control
       matches the button underneath it. */
    appearance: none;
    background-image: linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 50%, currentColor 50%),
                      linear-gradient(135deg, currentColor 50%, transparent 50%);
    background-position: calc(100% - 1.1em) 1.05em, calc(100% - 0.8em) 1.05em;
    background-size: 0.35em 0.35em, 0.35em 0.35em;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
  }

  .aj-deal__form-component {
    display: block;
  }

  .aj-deal__button {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .aj-deal__details {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-block-start: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-deal__button {
      width: auto;
      min-width: 16rem;
    }
  }

  .aj-deal__soldout {
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 600;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .aj-deal--empty {
    padding-block: var(--padding-xl, 3rem);
    text-align: center;
  }

{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Yoink of the Day",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Shows whichever daily_deal metaobject entry is active right now. Hidden on the storefront when nothing is scheduled."
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Color scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "default_headline",
      "label": "Default headline",
      "default": "Yoink of the Day",
      "info": "Used when the metaobject entry has no headline of its own."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Countdown"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_countdown",
      "label": "Show countdown",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "countdown_heading",
      "label": "Countdown label",
      "default": "Deal ends in"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "reload_on_expire",
      "label": "Reload when the deal ends",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Refreshes 5 seconds after the clock hits zero so the next deal loads."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Claimed bar"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_claimed",
      "label": "Show % claimed",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Calculated from real inventory against the units allocated on the metaobject. Hidden automatically when the product does not track inventory."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "When it shows is set once for the whole store, in Theme settings → Deal urgency, so the homepage and the product page cannot disagree."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "Top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 48
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "Bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 48
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Yoink of the Day"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
